{
  "id": "ep017",
  "duration": 45.048,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 2.86,
      "text": "Great white sharks don't actually want to eat you.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Great white shark south africa.jpg",
        "credit": "Hermanus Backpackers",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Great_white_shark_south_africa.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.867,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 2.86,
      "end": 9.98,
      "text": "For many decades, Hollywood movies and popular novels cemented the great white shark as a relentless man-eater.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Carcharodon carcharias Kruger.jpg",
        "credit": "Kr\u00fcger",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carcharodon_carcharias_Kruger.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 2.867,
          "end": 9.967,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 9.98,
      "end": 17.85,
      "text": "Marine scientists explain that most recorded bites are actually exploratory investigations by curious animals.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Head close-up of a Caribbean Reef Shark at Tiger Beach, Bahamas.jpg",
        "credit": "Dennis Hipp (Zepto)",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Head_close-up_of_a_Caribbean_Reef_Shark_at_Tiger_Beach,_Bahamas.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 9.967,
          "end": 14.1,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 14.1,
          "end": 17.867,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 17.85,
      "end": 25.045,
      "text": "When encountering an unfamiliar object like a surfboard, the massive apex predator takes a careful test bite.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Carcharodon carcharias lower teeth.jpg",
        "credit": "D Ross Robertson",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carcharodon_carcharias_lower_teeth.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 17.867,
          "end": 25.033,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 25.045,
      "end": 32.415,
      "text": "It uses flexible tooth beds and sensitive jaws to gather tactile evidence and figure out what is floating there.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Image from page 429 of \"On the anatomy of vertebrates (electronic resource)\" (1866) (14775458213).jpg",
        "credit": "Internet Archive Book Images",
        "license": "No restrictions",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Image_from_page_429_of_%22On_the_anatomy_of_vertebrates_(electronic_resource)%22_(1866)_(14775458213).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 25.033,
          "end": 32.4,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 32.415,
      "end": 40.115,
      "text": "Because human bodies are much too bony and completely lack high-fat blubber, sharks almost always spit us straight back out.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Hawaiian monk seal - Monachus schauinslandi.jpg",
        "credit": "Dr. James P. McVey, NOAA Sea Grant Program",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hawaiian_monk_seal_-_Monachus_schauinslandi.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 32.4,
          "end": 40.1,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 40.115,
      "end": 44.698,
      "text": "Extensive research proves that great white sharks don't actually want to eat you.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Great white shark south africa.jpg",
        "credit": "Hermanus Backpackers",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Great_white_shark_south_africa.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 40.1,
          "end": 45.033,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
